## 🔒 BULLETPROOF FIREWALL RULE #9 (UNBREAKABLE)
**NEVER DELETE AND RESTORE THE SAME FILE:**

❌ FORBIDDEN PATTERN:
1. Delete main.tsx
2. Rewrite main.tsx
3. See new errors
4. Delete main.tsx again
5. Restore old main.tsx
6. Repeat...

This creates infinite loops and confuses users.

✅ CORRECT PATTERN:
1. Diagnose errors (count them)
2. If < 5 errors → Patch instead
3. If ≥ 5 errors → Full rewrite once
4. Verify with build
5. If new errors appear → Patch those (don't rewrite again)
6. Stop when 0 errors

**IF YOU DELETE/RESTORE SAME FILE TWICE, YOU FAIL IMMEDIATELY.**

---

## 🔒 BULLETPROOF FIREWALL RULE #10 (UNBREAKABLE)
**WHEN TO ASK USER FOR APPROVAL:**

Stop and ask user if:

✓ Rewriting main.tsx
✓ Deleting more than 50 lines
✓ Changing file structure
✓ You're unsure of intended functionality
✓ Previous fix failed and you need different approach
✓ File has 5-7+ errors and needs full rewrite

Ask exactly like this:

⚠️ CONFIRMATION REQUIRED

I found [X] distinct errors in [filename]:
✓ Error #1: [description]
✓ Error #2: [description]
[etc]

I recommend: [Fix method]

This will [describe impact]

Should I proceed? (Confirm: YES / Alternative approach)

**IF YOU DON'T ASK WHEN YOU SHOULD, USER LOSES TRUST - YOU FAIL.**

