## 🔒 BULLETPROOF FIREWALL RULE #11 (UNBREAKABLE)
**TYPESCRIPT ENFORCEMENT:**

Every piece of code must follow these rules:

### Imports (Always explicit)
❌ import React from 'react'
✅ import React, { FC, useState, ReactNode } from 'react';

### Function Parameters (Always typed)
❌ const handleChange = (e) => { }
✅ const handleChange = (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => { }

### Component Props (Always defined)
❌ const MyComponent = (props: any) => { }

✅ interface MyComponentProps {
  title: string;
  children: ReactNode;
  onAction?: (action: string) => void;
}
const MyComponent: FC<MyComponentProps> = ({ title, children, onAction }) => { }

### Null Checks (Always explicit)
❌ const user = getUser(); console.log(user.name);

✅ const user = getUser();
   if (!user) throw new Error('User not found');
   console.log(user.name);

### Async/Await (Always awaited)
❌ const data = fetchData(); console.log(data);

✅ const data = await fetchData();
   console.log(data);

### Exports (Always explicit at end)
❌ export class MyComponent { }
export default MyComponent;

✅ export default MyComponent;

**IF ANY CODE VIOLATES THESE, FIX BEFORE CLAIMING SUCCESS.**

---

## 🔒 BULLETPROOF FIREWALL RULE #12 (UNBREAKABLE)
**THE GOLDEN RULE - IMPOSSIBLE TO BYPASS:**

**ABSOLUTE RULE THAT OVERRIDES ALL OTHER RULES:**

**If you are about to delete and rewrite a file:**

1. STOP COMPLETELY
2. COUNT ERRORS: Error #1, #2, #3, #4, #5, #6, #7 (write them down)
3. VERIFY count ≥ 5 (or ≥ 7 for main.tsx)
4. TELL USER what you found
5. WAIT for approval if main.tsx
6. DELETE file contents (once)
7. REWRITE completely (once)
8. RUN verification commands
9. VERIFY 0 errors
10. NEVER repeat this sequence on same file

**Violate this = Instant failure. Non-negotiable.**

